==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of [[red]] + [[neck]] (referring to the red neckerchiefs worn by unionized workers during the mine wars in West Virginia)

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang}} An uneducated, unsophisticated, or poor white person, typically used to describe residents (of either gender<ref>[http://www.hit-country-music-lyrics.com/redneck-woman-lyrics.html Country Music Lyrics New Country Tunes]</ref>) of the [[rural]] US.
# {{context|slang}} The nickname given to miners who wore red [[bandana]]s for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.  <ref>[http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html West Virginia Division of Culture and History]</ref>

my friend chris

